      "body": "<!--\r\nThank you for reporting an issue.\r\n\r\nThis issue tracker is for bugs and issues found within Node.js core.\r\nIf you require more general support please file an issue on our help\r\nrepo. https://github.com/nodejs/help\r\n\r\n\r\nPlease fill in as much of the template below as you're able.\r\n\r\nVersion: output of `node -v \r\nPlatform: output of `uname -a` (UNIX), or output of `\"$([Environment]::OSVersion | ForEach-Object VersionString) $(if ([Environment]::Is64BitOperatingSystem) { \"x64\" } else { \"x86\" })\"` in PowerShell console (Windows) window 10\r\nSubsystem: if known, please specify affected core module name: \r\n-->\r\n\r\n* **Version**:15.2.1\r\n* **Platform**:window 10\r\n* **Subsystem**:IMPORT\r\n\r\n### What steps will reproduce the bug?\r\n\r\n**a.js**\r\n```js\r\nimport {b} from \"./B.js\";\r\n```\r\n**b.js**\r\n\r\n```js\r\nexport {b};\r\nconst b = 10;\r\n```\r\n\r\n**package.json**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\r\n  \"type\": \"module\",\r\n  \"private\": true\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### How often does it reproduce? Is there a required condition?\r\n\r\nAlways\r\n\r\n### What is the expected behavior?\r\n\r\nB.js not found (Uppercase)\r\n\r\n### What do you see instead?\r\n\r\nno errors\r\n\r\n### Additional information\r\n\r\nIt creates error on linux",
